# The docker build context is runtime/ (provision/build_images.sh runs `docker build … .`
# from here). Both Dockerfiles COPY named paths only, so nothing below is needed in an image;
# without this file it is still uploaded to the docker daemon on every build.
#
# API keys reach a container at RUN time, never at build time: launch_rollout.py writes
# hosts/<rollout>/runner.env and agent.env, and host/compose.yaml.tmpl loads them with
# env_file. Keeping them out of the build context means a careless `COPY . .` added later
# cannot bake a key into an image (and from there into an AMI).
#
# NOTE hosts/ (per-rollout staging, holds secrets) is ignored; host/ (scripts) is NOT —
# Dockerfile.runner COPYs host/final_evaluation_snapshot.sh.
.env
.env.*
hosts/
campaigns/
runs/
scaffolds/
**/__pycache__/
